Your project uses **MSTest v3 (3.8.0)** on net8.0. Here's what to expect upgrading to **MSTest v4 (4.1.0)**:

## Breaking Changes That Affect Your Code

**`[ExpectedException]` removed** (lines 9, 16) — This is the main issue in your project. Replace with `Assert.ThrowsExactly<T>()`:

```csharp
// Before
[ExpectedException(typeof(ArgumentNullException))]
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Validate(null);
}

// After
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(() => Validate(null));
}
```

## Other Breaking Changes (not in your code, but good to know)

| Change | Fix |
|--------|-----|
| `Assert.ThrowsException` removed | Use `Assert.ThrowsExactly` |
| `[TestMethod("name")]` constructor changed | Use `DisplayName = "name"` |
| `ClassCleanupBehavior` enum removed | Remove argument from `[ClassCleanup]` |
| `TestContext.Properties.Contains` | Use `.ContainsKey()` |
| `TestTimeout.Infinite` removed | Use `int.MaxValue` |
| Custom `TestMethodAttribute.Execute` | Override `ExecuteAsync` instead |

## Behavioral Changes (no build errors, but watch for)

- **TreatDiscoveryWarningsAsErrors** now defaults to `true`
- **TestCase.Id** generation changed (Azure DevOps history may reset)
- Analyzer severities upgraded (new warnings possible)

